# Line endings, said out loud rather than left to whatever core.autocrlf a clone happens to have.
#
# Everything is normalized to LF in the repository. The working tree gets CRLF for the files a Windows editor
# touches - which is what .editorconfig declares - and LF for the two kinds that are read inside the Linux
# container, where a stray CR is taken as part of the value rather than as encoding, and for the hook, which is a
# shell script that has to run on a clone of any platform.
#
# Keep this in step with .editorconfig: where both name a file type, they must say the same thing.

* text=auto

*.cs text eol=crlf
*.csproj text eol=crlf
*.slnx text eol=crlf
*.props text eol=crlf
*.targets text eol=crlf
*.md text eol=crlf
*.json text eol=crlf
*.yml text eol=crlf
.editorconfig text eol=crlf
.gitignore text eol=crlf

Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.cf text eol=lf
.githooks/** text eol=lf

*.png binary
